stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> ToDo : yt issue create

    state "To do" as ToDo
    state "In Progress" as InProg
    state "Done" as Done

    ToDo --> InProg : yt issue apply 'State In Progress' (before first edit)
    InProg --> InProg : commit references issue as bare #KEY-N (link only, no State command), open PR
    InProg --> Done : human merges PR, then yt issue apply 'State Done' (explicit, post-merge)
    Done --> [*]

    note right of InProg
        Commit trailers are applied when the VCS integration parses the
        pushed commit, not on PR merge. A bare #KEY-N links the PR to the
        issue without transitioning it, so the issue stays In Progress
        through review. State Done is a deliberate post-merge action via
        yt issue apply, never a commit trailer.
    end note
